{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>עמל</b>. The fool is like one who sets out to seek great and wondrous things beyond himself, yet he does not know the visible and the known things — like a man who wants to go to a city but does not know the way; he toils and will not attain his desire. And every עמל in Scripture is masculine; this alone is feminine, like כל כבוד in Scripture being masculine except for one: אל תחד כבודי."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:59.612220827Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}